WEBVTT

01:44.104 --> 01:45.814
<i>What's Baki doing?</i>

01:45.897 --> 01:47.816
<i>He's letting him get too close!</i>

01:47.899 --> 01:50.568
<i>Is he even conscious?!</i>

01:52.570 --> 01:54.989
He slapped him.

01:55.073 --> 01:57.826
<i>That's... that's all I can do!</i>

01:58.952 --> 02:01.204
<i>The impact of falling from 30 meters</i>

02:02.455 --> 02:03.957
<i>It's just like the time I fell</i>

02:04.040 --> 02:06.459
<i>from the top of the jungle gym
when I was a kid</i>

02:07.335 --> 02:10.463
<i>or the time
I went flying off of the swing.</i>

02:12.215 --> 02:15.760
<i>It's like getting hammered
in the solar plexus by a powerful kick.</i>

02:16.553 --> 02:17.595
<i>Incredible pain.</i>

02:18.263 --> 02:19.514
<i>Difficulty breathing.</i>

02:20.223 --> 02:23.476
<i>I can feel my internal organs
are in total chaos</i>

02:23.560 --> 02:25.436
<i>from the shock of hitting the ground.</i>

02:26.729 --> 02:29.858
<i>My diaphragm's being forced up
as far as it'll go.</i>

02:29.941 --> 02:31.568
<i>It's crushing my lungs.</i>

02:32.443 --> 02:35.280
<i>Which explains why
I'm barely able to suck in any oxygen.</i>

02:39.784 --> 02:42.078
<i>That salty taste</i>.

02:44.956 --> 02:46.207
<i>Metallic smell.</i>

02:46.958 --> 02:48.042
<i>That's blood!</i>

02:50.420 --> 02:51.880
<i>I'm spitting up blood!</i>

02:52.589 --> 02:54.299
<i>That means major organ damage!</i>

02:55.717 --> 02:57.594
<i>I feel like I wanna fall to my knees!</i>

02:58.595 --> 03:00.054
<i>Collapse on the ground!</i>

03:00.138 --> 03:03.016
<i>It's like my legs
are holding up a giant rock!</i>

03:03.099 --> 03:05.518
<i>And I just wanna let it crush me!</i>

03:05.602 --> 03:07.854
<i>No matter how tough Baki is,</i>

03:07.937 --> 03:11.900
<i>falling from that height,
it's more than any human could endure.</i>

03:13.568 --> 03:16.029
<i>There's no way he wasn't hurt.</i>

03:16.112 --> 03:18.156
<i>I'm surprised he can even stand.</i>

03:20.491 --> 03:23.077
<i>But the primitive man
saw through him.</i>

03:23.703 --> 03:28.583
<i>His playmate might appear to be fine
and as uninjured as he himself was,</i>

03:29.250 --> 03:30.835
<i>but it was camouflage.</i>

03:31.461 --> 03:33.296
<i>Pickle could sense the truth,</i>

03:33.796 --> 03:36.799
<i>that the man had suffered
grave physical damage.</i>

03:38.384 --> 03:41.262
<i>Though he stood there
looking like he was ready to fight,</i>

03:41.346 --> 03:44.641
<i>inside, he was writhing in pain.</i>

03:46.184 --> 03:48.186
<i>What are you waiting for Pickle?</i>

03:49.771 --> 03:50.939
<i>Strike me down!</i>

03:51.606 --> 03:52.815
<i>I'm defenseless!</i>

03:54.484 --> 03:56.778
<i>The primitive man felt regret.</i>

03:57.612 --> 04:00.490
<i>Don't just stand there, damn it.
Punch me!</i>

04:00.573 --> 04:01.491
<i>Kick me!</i>

04:02.075 --> 04:03.243
<i>He said to himself...</i>

04:03.326 --> 04:05.078
<i>Now's your chance!</i>

04:05.870 --> 04:07.455
<i>..."I have gone too far.”</i>

04:09.374 --> 04:11.417
<i>“I treated this plaything too roughly."</i>

04:12.001 --> 04:13.294
<i>"I injured him.”</i>

04:20.093 --> 04:21.636
<i>“Please get better.”</i>

04:24.597 --> 04:27.892
<i>The humiliation
of seeing his opponent pray for him</i>

04:28.393 --> 04:30.228
<i>was too much for the young man.</i>

04:31.104 --> 04:33.022
<i>And so his pride took over...</i>

04:33.815 --> 04:36.776
Don't you fuckin' pray me for me!

04:38.653 --> 04:41.739
<i>He momentarily forgot
the overwhelming pain.</i>

04:42.615 --> 04:44.200
<i>But his lungs had been crushed,</i>

04:44.701 --> 04:46.744
<i>and he found that he could hardly speak.</i>

04:49.747 --> 04:52.125
Don't you fuckin' pray!

05:03.553 --> 05:04.679
C'mon.

05:05.680 --> 05:06.639
Come at me!

05:07.473 --> 05:09.350
Stupid son of a bitch!

05:11.436 --> 05:13.062
Uh-oh, here it comes!!

05:17.608 --> 05:18.484
<i>Huh?</i>

05:33.249 --> 05:34.208
What?

05:34.709 --> 05:37.462
What in the world
is Pickle doing out there now?

05:38.004 --> 05:40.173
<i>Tokugawa may not
have understood,</i>

05:40.673 --> 05:43.343
<i>but the experienced fighters
knew what it meant.</i>

05:43.426 --> 05:44.594
It's too much.

05:45.887 --> 05:47.597
I can't bear to watch.

05:49.807 --> 05:51.017
What the...

05:52.268 --> 05:54.520
<i>Pickle tried
to show him it was okay.</i>

05:55.813 --> 05:58.983
<i>You see? They're not dangerous.</i>

05:59.067 --> 06:00.693
<i>Everyone's afraid of them,</i>

06:00.777 --> 06:03.905
<i>but you're perfectly safe
when I use them like this.</i>

06:08.284 --> 06:09.911
You bastard...

06:09.994 --> 06:11.871
<i>All right now?</i>

06:12.622 --> 06:13.915
<i>Then let's play!</i>

06:14.540 --> 06:15.708
<i>Play with me.</i>

06:16.417 --> 06:20.338
<i>Baki saw that Pickle was pretending
his fists weren't lethal weapons.</i>

06:21.923 --> 06:23.216
<i>In the past,</i>

06:23.299 --> 06:26.302
<i>Baki's endorphins had been triggered
by physical damage</i>

06:26.386 --> 06:28.805
<i>or the danger of physical damage.</i>

06:29.430 --> 06:34.102
<i>But now, it was the absence of danger
that his brain reacted to.</i>

06:34.685 --> 06:37.647
<i>Pickle's playful blows
would not have hurt a fly.</i>

06:38.314 --> 06:41.275
<i>But they had struck Baki
in his weakest point.</i>

06:45.488 --> 06:48.074
<i>They had hit him
where it hurts the most.</i>

06:48.157 --> 06:49.409
<i>In his pride.</i>

06:50.535 --> 06:52.286
<i>This wasn't anyone's fault.</i>

06:54.414 --> 06:55.373
Hold on.

06:55.456 --> 06:57.083
What's he doing?

06:59.627 --> 07:02.088
<i>I was just too weak,</i>

07:02.630 --> 07:03.589
<i>that's all.</i>

07:04.632 --> 07:06.259
You fool!

07:07.718 --> 07:09.262
<i>I'm sorry, Pickle.</i>

07:12.723 --> 07:14.350
It's suicide!

07:15.560 --> 07:17.854
<i>I'm sorry
I made you worried about me.</i>

07:18.938 --> 07:20.815
<i>I'm the one who started this fight.</i>

07:22.692 --> 07:24.777
<i>I'm the one who provoked you.</i>

07:25.445 --> 07:28.281
<i>And yet you ended up having to pity me.</i>

07:41.878 --> 07:44.088
I know you've been around longer than me

07:44.881 --> 07:47.258
by millions and millions of years.

07:51.429 --> 07:53.890
But I don't need your pity, old man.

07:53.973 --> 07:55.850
What is Baki doing?

07:56.893 --> 07:58.853
Reckless little fool.

07:58.936 --> 08:00.313
Unbelievable.

08:03.983 --> 08:06.235
<i>Was this more camouflage?</i>

08:07.278 --> 08:08.779
<i>Pickle was confused.</i>

08:09.530 --> 08:14.202
<i>He knew that camouflage was used
by things pretending to be dead,</i>

08:14.744 --> 08:16.621
<i>or feigning weakness,</i>

08:16.704 --> 08:20.625
<i>or by things trying to trick your eyes
in order to avoid detection.</i>

08:21.918 --> 08:24.295
<i>Camouflage was used for survival.</i>

08:25.171 --> 08:28.799
<i>And yet, Pickle had seen this man
repeat that same action</i>

08:28.883 --> 08:31.552
<i>that had so badly hurt him
in the first place,</i>

08:31.636 --> 08:36.140
<i>thereby increasing the damage
to his already gravely injured body.</i>

08:37.642 --> 08:40.228
<i>Can such a camouflage as this exist?</i>

08:41.103 --> 08:42.897
<i>Could death be a camouflage?</i>

08:45.107 --> 08:47.276
<i>Can such a being exist?</i>

08:47.777 --> 08:50.154
<i>The weak eats the mighty?</i>

08:53.199 --> 08:55.785
And after all that, Baki missed him!

08:56.369 --> 08:58.746
<i>There's no way
he could've recovered.</i>

08:59.664 --> 09:00.706
Wait a minute--

09:12.593 --> 09:14.470
Pickle's down!

09:35.157 --> 09:37.118
What? But how?

09:37.201 --> 09:39.036
Baki didn't even touch him, did he?

09:39.120 --> 09:40.413
Retsu.

09:41.163 --> 09:43.249
what exactly is happening here?

09:45.626 --> 09:47.461
I can't speak with certainty.

09:48.504 --> 09:49.839
But I have an idea.

09:51.090 --> 09:53.009
<i>Whether it's ancient dinosaurs</i>

09:53.092 --> 09:55.511
<i>or the best modern fighters,</i>

09:55.595 --> 09:57.221
<i>nothing has been able to deliver</i>

09:57.305 --> 10:00.891
<i>a blow strong enough to overcome
the resilience of Pickle's body.</i>

10:01.559 --> 10:05.062
<i>I think Baki realized
that no direct blow with foot or fist</i>

10:05.146 --> 10:07.773
<i>would ever shake that primeval brain.</i>

10:08.899 --> 10:10.234
That's why he struck him

10:11.611 --> 10:13.738
with just the surface of the skin.

10:14.322 --> 10:15.448
The what?

10:15.531 --> 10:16.574
Hmm.

10:17.950 --> 10:19.744
The punch doesn't land.

10:20.369 --> 10:22.371
It only grazes the chin.

10:23.289 --> 10:26.834
<i>It's a technique used in the boxing ring,
albeit rarely.</i>

10:26.917 --> 10:29.378
<i>A sudden flick of a boxer's glove,</i>

10:29.462 --> 10:31.714
<i>so quick it's mistaken for a miss,</i>

10:31.797 --> 10:33.591
<i>and the other boxer goes down.</i>

10:33.674 --> 10:34.508
<i>Sometimes,</i>

10:35.134 --> 10:36.969
never to get up again.

10:37.053 --> 10:41.432
Hmm! True, unexplainable knockouts
like that have been known to happen.

10:42.141 --> 10:45.394
It is unexpected and effective.

10:46.103 --> 10:48.773
<i>Someone who can withstand
a punch through a cushion</i>

10:48.856 --> 10:51.609
<i>will black out
when only the cushion is struck.</i>

10:53.653 --> 10:57.114
<i>A thin layer of skin
on the unguarded jaw is just grazed,</i>

10:57.198 --> 11:00.076
<i>but the blow is so fast
that it shakes the jaw,</i>

11:00.159 --> 11:02.495
<i>and, imperceptibly, the brain,</i>

11:02.578 --> 11:05.665
<i>at a super high speed
invisible to the naked eye.</i>

11:10.294 --> 11:12.713
So he didn't miss him.

11:13.506 --> 11:15.841
No, he hit him, but only with this.

11:16.342 --> 11:17.927
The surface of the skin.

11:18.010 --> 11:19.887
<i>Once with his left fist,</i>

11:19.970 --> 11:21.847
<i>once with his right fist,</i>

11:21.931 --> 11:23.808
<i>and once with the heel of his foot.</i>

11:24.558 --> 11:27.978
<i>No doubt Pickle's brain
started vibrating with the first blow,</i>

11:28.062 --> 11:29.647
<i>and the speed of the vibrations</i>

11:29.730 --> 11:32.817
<i>would have been increased
by the second and third blows.</i>

11:33.651 --> 11:34.902
<i>The result was,</i>

11:34.985 --> 11:37.321
<i>he lost the normal functioning
of his brain,</i>

11:37.905 --> 11:40.741
<i>which must have been very puzzling
and alarming to Pickle.</i>

11:41.409 --> 11:44.537
<i>One minute he's untouched,
unhurt, and standing upright,</i>

11:44.620 --> 11:47.873
<i>and the next minute,
the ground is coming up to meet him.</i>

11:50.251 --> 11:53.629
That attack would have been something
completely outside his experience.

11:53.713 --> 11:54.630
Huh.

11:55.172 --> 11:56.549
Whoa.

11:56.632 --> 11:59.760
Pickle's in a state
of utter confusion right now.

12:01.303 --> 12:04.098
<i>It was just
as Sea King Retsu surmised.</i>

12:04.181 --> 12:06.600
<i>Dazed by a blow he hadn't even felt,</i>

12:06.684 --> 12:09.270
<i>Pickle now saw, standing there before him,</i>

12:09.353 --> 12:11.522
<i>a man who had been on the verge of death,</i>

12:11.605 --> 12:14.275
<i>who hadn't even begun
to recover from his injuries...</i>

12:14.358 --> 12:17.737
<i>This man had transformed himself
into a sorcerer</i>

12:17.820 --> 12:20.239
<i>who could control
the ground beneath their feet.</i>

12:20.990 --> 12:23.284
<i>Pickle's whole body was trembling.</i>

12:23.784 --> 12:26.120
<i>But still, he did not run.</i>

12:28.164 --> 12:29.749
<i>He had overcome blows.</i>

12:30.541 --> 12:31.876
<i>He had overcome weight.</i>

12:32.918 --> 12:34.295
<i>He had overcome strength.</i>

12:34.795 --> 12:36.714
<i>He had overcome danger.</i>

12:37.673 --> 12:39.467
<i>He had even overcome that.</i>

12:40.676 --> 12:45.598
<i>A sense of invincibility was engraved
in every particle of his being.</i>

12:47.725 --> 12:48.976
<i>He had come here,</i>

12:49.477 --> 12:50.644
<i>and been challenged</i>

12:50.728 --> 12:54.231
<i>by small men with the strength of giants.</i>

12:54.815 --> 12:56.817
<i>And he had overcome pain too.</i>

12:59.737 --> 13:01.280
<i>But this was different.</i>

13:01.864 --> 13:05.534
<i>This was a new experience,
beyond his comprehension.</i>

13:07.119 --> 13:09.455
<i>The unprecedented experience</i>

13:09.538 --> 13:11.874
<i>of his body slamming into the ground,</i>

13:12.875 --> 13:13.876
<i>twice...</i>

13:15.085 --> 13:18.881
<i>Pickle couldn't do that,
make the ground move like that.</i>

13:19.381 --> 13:21.550
<i>He'd never thought of making it move.</i>

13:22.301 --> 13:24.678
<i>Even that thing couldn't make it move.</i>

13:25.471 --> 13:27.014
<i>But he could.</i>

13:27.515 --> 13:29.767
<i>The primitive man knew
he would barely be able</i>

13:29.850 --> 13:34.188
<i>to hold his own against this little giant
who could move the ground.</i>

13:34.271 --> 13:36.106
<i>No.</i>

13:36.857 --> 13:40.861
<i>I still haven't recovered
from the first fall, let alone the second.</i>

13:41.987 --> 13:44.907
<i>I can't attack him head-on, not yet.</i>

13:51.705 --> 13:53.707
<i>Sorry about this, Pickle...</i>

13:54.250 --> 13:56.961
Is he doing what I think he's doing ?

13:57.461 --> 13:59.421
<i>Wish I didn't have to,</i>

14:00.047 --> 14:02.383
<i>but I'm gonna do something
that's a little bit mean.</i>

14:02.466 --> 14:05.094
I can't believe I'm only seeing it now.

14:06.220 --> 14:09.223
<i>Why didn't I think of that
when I was fighting with Pickle?!</i>

14:11.392 --> 14:13.769
Baki, my boy, you're a born genius.

14:26.240 --> 14:28.784
<i>That's what hell
feels like, Pickle.</i>

14:34.748 --> 14:36.208
Look at the pain he's in,

14:36.792 --> 14:38.878
in spite of all his toughness.

14:45.843 --> 14:48.721
Look at the mark
Baki's hand left on his back!

14:49.513 --> 14:51.515
Hmm. Can you explain that one?

14:52.266 --> 14:54.894
That one's a killer.

14:56.270 --> 14:58.147
It's known as the "hip Strike,"

14:58.230 --> 15:02.109
and it has the same effect on everyone,
from infants to Yujiro Hanma.

15:02.693 --> 15:05.738
It's taught in the Japanese art of <i>Kudo.</i>

15:06.322 --> 15:08.282
It's a hybrid form of martial arts.

15:08.908 --> 15:11.577
In kung fu, it's known as Columbus's Egg.

15:12.202 --> 15:15.205
The muscles are relaxed
until they're loose and flaccid.

15:15.289 --> 15:18.459
Every part of the body
goes completely limp.

15:18.542 --> 15:21.545
<i>Strangely enough,
as the body is made loose,</i>

15:21.629 --> 15:24.048
<i>the hands and feet increase in weight.</i>

15:25.132 --> 15:28.510
<i>At last, when even the tension
in the face has disappeared,</i>

15:28.594 --> 15:30.346
<i>the body becomes a whip!</i>

15:32.222 --> 15:34.391
<i>At this point,
it's no longer a question</i>

15:34.475 --> 15:36.518
<i>of looking for an opponent's weak spots.</i>

15:38.938 --> 15:40.856
<i>Because now
the target of the attack</i>

15:40.940 --> 15:44.526
<i>is the largest organ
of the human body, the skin.</i>

15:45.402 --> 15:48.530
<i>Whether it's the skin
of a hardened, well-honed warrior,</i>

15:49.031 --> 15:51.283
<i>or the soft flesh of a young maiden,</i>

15:51.367 --> 15:56.205
<i>a blow to it from a perfectly flaccid hand
is equally painful.</i>

15:56.872 --> 16:00.417
- Take a punch to the face, Hanayama.
- What?

16:00.501 --> 16:04.713
It's going to hurt you less
than it would, say, a small child, right?

16:05.839 --> 16:07.091
But with a slap,

16:07.174 --> 16:09.551
it doesn't matter whether you're a child

16:10.219 --> 16:13.222
or the unconquerable Kaoru Hanayama,

16:13.722 --> 16:16.016
the intensity of the pain
will be the same.

16:16.100 --> 16:17.893
You may be right.

16:17.977 --> 16:19.186
You are right.

16:23.190 --> 16:26.235
And yet,
in the entire history of life on Earth,

16:26.860 --> 16:28.696
<i>from two billion years ago,</i>

16:28.779 --> 16:30.614
<i>when proteins began the mutations</i>

16:30.698 --> 16:33.534
<i>that would ultimately result
in human beings...</i>

16:34.451 --> 16:36.328
Where are you going with this?

16:36.412 --> 16:40.290
...of the many millions of creatures
that have developed over that time...

16:40.374 --> 16:43.419
You are going to get
to the point eventually, I hope.

16:43.919 --> 16:46.255
...has there ever been
another living creature

16:46.338 --> 16:50.175
<i>that transformed itself into a whip
and targeted the skin?</i>

16:51.635 --> 16:53.929
No. Not that I can think of.

16:54.513 --> 16:56.849
<i>Was that
a metaphorical question?</i>

16:58.058 --> 17:00.602
On second thought,
perhaps there is one creature.

17:01.437 --> 17:03.022
The human female.

17:03.522 --> 17:06.358
Women have been known to do it.

17:06.442 --> 17:09.278
Oh. Like a slap in the face, you mean?

17:09.361 --> 17:10.821
Yes, they'll do that.

17:12.865 --> 17:15.242
Oh! Will you look at that!

17:15.325 --> 17:18.495
I've never seen Pickle
in such a defensive posture before!

17:21.290 --> 17:23.667
Even he has to defend himself.

17:24.418 --> 17:26.128
For him, this situation

17:26.712 --> 17:29.006
is like nothing
he's ever had to face before.

17:32.134 --> 17:34.511
That's it, Baki! You've done it!

17:34.595 --> 17:37.514
You've got that caveman on the ropes now!

17:38.140 --> 17:40.726
No, I don't think so.

17:43.979 --> 17:46.398
Baki's attack stung him badly,

17:46.482 --> 17:49.109
but it stung his pride even more!

17:49.693 --> 17:51.153
Look at that!

17:51.236 --> 17:53.113
Retsu! You see what he's doing?!

17:53.197 --> 17:54.448
I see it.

17:55.240 --> 17:59.119
That's what he did
right before he attacked me

17:59.203 --> 18:01.538
and brought our match to an end.

18:03.791 --> 18:07.252
And there's no using
the Whip Strike again.

18:07.961 --> 18:08.962
That's right.

18:09.505 --> 18:12.800
But I suspect
that Baki is fully aware of that already.

18:20.474 --> 18:21.934
What?

18:22.434 --> 18:24.853
Again? The Whip Strike?

18:24.937 --> 18:27.815
Huh? Has he run out of tricks?

18:28.315 --> 18:30.150
How does he think that's gonna work?

18:30.234 --> 18:32.820
Pickle will flatten him
before he can even use it!

18:33.403 --> 18:34.279
Hold on.

18:35.405 --> 18:36.824
That's something else...

18:41.036 --> 18:41.995
<i>Kokeiken?!</i>

18:42.079 --> 18:43.997
What's <i>"Kokeiken"</i>?

18:44.081 --> 18:46.125
A style of kung fu

18:46.917 --> 18:49.670
that integrates the form
and strength of a tiger.

18:50.170 --> 18:52.756
But I don't understand.

18:53.340 --> 18:55.342
Why use king fu at this point?

19:00.973 --> 19:02.432
<i>Yosoken!</i>

19:04.560 --> 19:05.894
<i>Toroken!</i>

19:06.562 --> 19:07.980
<i>Saruken!</i>

19:09.064 --> 19:10.065
<i>Yushoken!</i>

19:10.566 --> 19:12.067
What the heck?

19:12.568 --> 19:16.196
Is there any actual fighting involved,
or does he just imitate animals?

19:16.864 --> 19:17.948
<i>Genius.</i>

19:18.448 --> 19:22.494
<i>His ability to master the integration
of so many different animals</i>

19:22.578 --> 19:25.080
<i>can only be described as genius.</i>

19:26.248 --> 19:28.333
<i>But I hope you haven't forgotten, Baki</i>

19:28.959 --> 19:32.129
<i>Of all those beasts
you've so perfectly emulated,</i>

19:32.212 --> 19:35.549
<i>there's not one of them
that wouldn't be prey for Pickle.</i>

19:36.967 --> 19:39.928
<i>Even if you did more
than just emulate them</i>

19:40.012 --> 19:42.598
<i>and actually transformed
into those animals,</i>

19:42.681 --> 19:45.851
<i>they could never win against that savage.</i>

19:55.152 --> 19:56.236
<i>What's this?</i>

19:56.820 --> 19:58.655
<i>What are you going to emulate next?</i>

20:02.367 --> 20:04.244
<i>This is an animal as well.</i>

20:04.745 --> 20:05.579
<i>But what?</i>

20:06.371 --> 20:07.539
<i>Whatever it is,</i>

20:08.165 --> 20:09.333
<i>it's strong</i>

20:09.917 --> 20:11.210
<i>Incredibly strong</i>

20:11.877 --> 20:13.045
<i>And big.</i>

20:13.128 --> 20:14.254
<i>Enormous.</i>

20:14.838 --> 20:17.716
<i>An elephant? A rhino?</i>

20:17.799 --> 20:19.509
No.

20:19.593 --> 20:20.427
It can't be!

20:22.221 --> 20:23.680
<i>Triceratops!</i>

20:30.604 --> 20:33.148
<i>Pickle was utterly bewildered.</i>

20:34.066 --> 20:36.818
<i>This man was less than half his size.</i>

20:36.902 --> 20:40.530
<i>And yet, in this small,
supposedly helpless figure,</i>

20:41.198 --> 20:42.866
<i>he sensed he was facing</i>

20:42.950 --> 20:45.744
<i>the most powerful opponent
he'd ever known.</i>

20:46.703 --> 20:50.707
<i>The impression of boulder-like weight
and enormous power,</i>

20:51.416 --> 20:54.336
<i>as if a colossal tree
had learned how to move.</i>

20:55.379 --> 21:00.384
<i>The iron will that never wavers
until the enemy has been destroyed.</i>

21:01.635 --> 21:04.304
<i>Those things, all those things</i>

21:04.388 --> 21:05.847
<i>in this body.</i>

21:06.348 --> 21:09.226
<i>Here, in this little body,</i>

21:09.309 --> 21:11.478
<i>he could sense their presence.</i>

21:12.312 --> 21:13.689
It's incredible.

21:14.189 --> 21:17.192
I'd have never believed it
if I hadn't seen it myself.

21:17.276 --> 21:19.319
Baki's so small compared to Pickle.

21:19.403 --> 21:22.906
And yet with that one move,
he's got him completely intimidated!

21:23.490 --> 21:25.367
Size has nothing to do with it.

21:25.867 --> 21:28.078
I'm twice the size he is,

21:28.161 --> 21:30.038
and I couldn't do what he's doing.

21:30.122 --> 21:31.873
I don't think anyone could.

21:33.417 --> 21:36.545
What now?
Has he got something else up his sleeve?

21:36.628 --> 21:39.006
He's focusing upward,
toward the sky!

21:43.677 --> 21:47.097
Ooh, it's a flying bird!
Is that what he's doing?

21:49.850 --> 21:53.270
Whoo! That's a T. rex! I think.

21:55.647 --> 21:58.984
<i>Pickle had seen
this sorcerer move the ground.</i>

21:59.067 --> 22:01.653
<i>Now he watched him changing shapes.</i>

22:01.737 --> 22:04.740
<i>He could no longer envision
the man in his true form.</i>

22:05.615 --> 22:06.950
<i>In Pickle's eyes,</i>

22:07.034 --> 22:09.369
<i>he had been utterly transformed</i>

22:09.453 --> 22:12.414
<i>into the mightiest beasts
that roamed the Earth.</i>

22:12.497 --> 22:15.125
It's truly incredible.

22:17.669 --> 22:20.505
It's like magic.
